{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T12:25:38.677045", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Map a textual direction to the corresponding action index.\n  # In CraftLab the actions are: DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3, USE=4.\n  dir_to_action = {\"down\": 0, \"up\": 1, \"left\": 2, \"right\": 3}\n  d = dir.lower()\n  actions = []\n  if d in dir_to_action:\n      # Move (and face) the desired direction.\n      actions.append(dir_to_action[d])\n      # Attempt to break the obstacle with the USE action.\n      actions.append(4)  # USE\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
