{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T12:32:09.114037", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple baseline: take random actions until the task is done or a step limit is reached.\n  actions = []\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit; use the environment's max_steps attribute if present.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Pre\u2011compute the list of possible action indices.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Stop if the environment reports completion.\n      if env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Sample a random action and execute it.\n      act = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      actions.append(int(act))\n\n      # If the environment signals termination, exit early.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
