{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T12:40:35.916101", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  # Prepare a list to record the sequence of actions taken.\n  actions_taken = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable limit on the number of steps.\n  # Many CraftLab environments expose `max_steps`; if not, fall back to a large default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Use the environment's random state if available; otherwise fall back to NumPy's RNG.\n  rng = getattr(env, \"random\", np.random.RandomState())\n\n  # Simple random policy: at each step choose a random action from the action space.\n  # Action indices are defined by CraftLab: 0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT, 4=USE.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      action = int(rng.randint(0, 5))  # Random integer in [0, 4]\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(action)\n      actions_taken.append(action)\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions that were executed.\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
