{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T12:44:40.113074", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy: reset the environment, then take random actions\n  # until the task is completed or the maximum number of steps is reached.\n  # Returns the list of action indices taken.\n  actions = []\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode\n  env.reset()\n  # Determine the set of possible action indices\n  action_space = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  # Use the max_steps attribute if present, otherwise fall back to a large default\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Stop if the environment reports completion\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n      # Choose a random action from the available actions\n      a = int(np.random.choice(action_space))\n      # Execute the action\n      _, done, _ = env.step(a)\n      actions.append(a)\n      # Exit early if the environment signals termination\n      if done:\n          break\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
