{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T12:48:51.437767", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Mapping from direction names to grid deltas\n  dir_to_delta = {\n      \"DOWN\": (1, 0),\n      \"UP\": (-1, 0),\n      \"LEFT\": (0, -1),\n      \"RIGHT\": (0, 1),\n  }\n\n  # Order in which we will scan directions\n  directions = [\"DOWN\", \"UP\", \"LEFT\", \"RIGHT\"]\n\n  # Current state and world information\n  state = env._current_state\n  world = env.world\n\n  # Set of indices that correspond to non\u2011grabbable (obstacle) entities\n  obstacle_kinds = set(world.non_grabbable_indices)\n\n  # Grid dimensions\n  width, height, _ = state.grid.shape\n\n  # Scan neighboring cells for an obstacle\n  for d in directions:\n      dx, dy = dir_to_delta[d]\n      nx, ny = state.pos[0] + dx, state.pos[1] + dy\n\n      # Bounds check\n      if not (0 <= nx < width and 0 <= ny < height):\n          continue\n\n      # The cell is a one\u2011hot vector over kinds; find the present kind (if any)\n      cell = state.grid[nx, ny]\n      if cell.sum() == 0:\n          continue  # empty cell\n\n      kind = int(np.argmax(cell))\n      if kind in obstacle_kinds:\n          # Found an obstacle in direction `d`; use the breaking routine\n          return break_func_v1(env, d)\n\n  # No adjacent obstacle found \u2013 return an empty action list\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 8, "scores": {}}
