{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T12:54:36.820423", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random\u2011action baseline.\n  # The function runs the environment until the task is completed\n  # (or a safety step limit is hit) and records the actions taken.\n  actions = []\n  # safety limit \u2013 prevents endless loops in case of bugs\n  MAX_STEPS = 1000\n\n  # Obtain the list of possible action integers once.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  for _ in range(MAX_STEPS):\n      # Stop if the task is already satisfied or max steps reached.\n      if env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Choose a random legal action.\n      act = env.world.random.choice(possible_actions)\n\n      # Record and execute the action.\n      actions.append(int(act))\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # If the environment reports termination, exit early.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
