{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T12:59:11.665320", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to a known state.\n  env.reset()\n\n  # Mapping from direction strings to action indices as defined in CraftLab.action_specs.\n  dir_to_action = {\n      \"DOWN\": 0,\n      \"UP\": 1,\n      \"LEFT\": 2,\n      \"RIGHT\": 3,\n  }\n\n  actions = []\n\n  # Turn (or attempt to move) towards the specified direction so that the agent\n  # faces the adjacent cell containing the obstacle.\n  if dir in dir_to_action:\n      actions.append(dir_to_action[dir])\n\n  # Use the tool (or bare hands) on the cell the agent is currently facing.\n  USE = 4\n  actions.append(USE)\n\n  # Apply the actions to keep the environment's internal state in sync.\n  for a in actions:\n      env.step(a)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 1, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
