{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:06:13.561289", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  actions = []\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit; use the environment's max_steps if available\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 200)\n\n  # Random policy: keep taking random actions until the task is completed or step limit reached\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # If the environment signals completion, stop early\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Sample a random action from the available action space\n      # CraftWorld stores the number of actions in `n_actions` and provides a RNG in `world.random`\n      n_actions = getattr(env.world, \"n_actions\", 5)  # default to 5 actions if not defined\n      action = int(env.world.random.randint(n_actions))\n\n      # Record and execute the action\n      actions.append(action)\n      # `step` may return (reward, done, obs) or just (reward, new_state); we ignore its output here\n      try:\n          env.step(action)\n      except Exception:\n          # If the environment's step signature differs, ignore the result\n          pass\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
