{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:09:12.884118", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import random\n\n  # Determine the set of possible actions from the environment's specification.\n  try:\n      action_space = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  except Exception:\n      # Fallback to the typical 5-action space if the spec is unavailable.\n      action_space = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n\n  # Use the environment's maximum step limit if it exists; otherwise cap at 1000.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Choose an action uniformly at random.\n      act = random.choice(action_space)\n      actions_taken.append(act)\n\n      # Execute the action; step returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # Stop early if the episode has terminated.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
