{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:09:34.695166", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  env.reset()\n\n  actions = []\n  # Upper bound on steps to avoid infinite loops in case the goal is unreachable.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # The simplest possible action: try to use the item directly in front of the agent.\n      # In many CraftWorld configurations a single USE action (index 4) is enough to\n      # collect adjacent primitives or trigger crafting when the required ingredients\n      # are already in the inventory.\n      act = 4  # USE\n      actions.append(act)\n\n      # Execute the action; the step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # Stop as soon as the environment reports that the episode is finished.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
