{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:22:33.042934", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  # Prepare a list to collect the sequence of actions taken.\n  actions = []\n  # Determine a maximum number of steps to avoid infinite loops.\n  # Use the environment's configured max_steps if available, otherwise fall back to a default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Main interaction loop: keep taking actions until the episode terminates or we hit the step limit.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # If the environment reports that the episode is done, exit the loop early.\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Choose a random valid action. The environment provides a mapping from action names to integer codes.\n      # We sample uniformly from the set of action codes.\n      action_codes = list(env.action_specs().values())\n      if not action_codes:\n          # No actions available; break out to avoid an error.\n          break\n      act = np.random.choice(action_codes)\n\n      # Record the chosen action.\n      actions.append(int(act))\n\n      # Execute the action in the environment. The step method typically returns\n      # (reward, done, observation). We ignore reward and observation here.\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # If the step indicated the episode is done, exit the loop.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the complete list of actions taken during this episode.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
