{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:23:43.931033", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  actions = []\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit (use the environment's max_steps if available)\n  step_limit = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 500)\n\n  for _ in range(step_limit):\n      # Stop if the task is already completed or the environment signals done\n      if getattr(env, \"_is_done\", lambda: False)():\n          break\n\n      # Sample a random valid action (0..n_actions-1)\n      n_actions = getattr(env.world, \"n_actions\", 5)  # default to 5 actions if missing\n      act = int(np.random.randint(0, n_actions))\n\n      # Execute the action\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      actions.append(act)\n\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
