{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:34:34.320869", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  _ = env.reset()\n\n  # Gather the possible action indices from the environment's action specification.\n  action_spec = env.action_specs()\n  possible_actions = list(action_spec.values())\n\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit.  Use the environment's max_steps attribute if present,\n  # otherwise fall back to a default large number.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Record the sequence of actions taken during the episode.\n  action_sequence = []\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Choose an action uniformly at random from the allowed set.\n      act = int(np.random.choice(possible_actions))\n      action_sequence.append(act)\n\n      # Perform the action; the step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # Terminate early if the episode is finished (goal achieved or step limit reached).\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return action_sequence", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
