{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:34:54.056287", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation\n  env.reset()\n\n  # Determine the set of possible action indices from the environment's action specification\n  action_spec = env.action_specs()\n  # action_spec is a dict mapping action names to integer indices\n  possible_actions = list(action_spec.values())\n\n  # List to record the sequence of actions taken\n  action_sequence = []\n\n  # Continue stepping through the environment until it signals that the episode is done\n  done = False\n  # Safety limit to avoid infinite loops in pathological cases\n  max_steps = 10000\n\n  while not done and len(action_sequence) < max_steps:\n      # Choose an action at random from the available actions\n      action = int(np.random.choice(possible_actions))\n      # Execute the action in the environment\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(action)\n      # Record the action taken\n      action_sequence.append(action)\n\n  # Return the recorded sequence of actions (as a list of integers)\n  return action_sequence", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
