{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:40:28.360668", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Retrieve the current CraftState from the environment.\n  state = getattr(env, \"_current_state\", None)\n  if state is None:\n      # No state available \u2013 cannot decide on actions.\n      return []\n\n  # Determine the direction the agent is currently facing.\n  # In CraftState, dir follows the same indexing as actions:\n  # 0=DOWN, 1=UP, 2=LEFT, 3=RIGHT.\n  dir_idx = state.dir\n  dir_str = {0: \"DOWN\", 1: \"UP\", 2: \"LEFT\", 3: \"RIGHT\"}.get(dir_idx, \"DOWN\")\n\n  # Try the available breaking strategies in order of sophistication.\n  for break_func in (break_func_v0, break_func_v1, break_func_v2):\n      actions = break_func(env, dir_str)\n      if actions:          # a non\u2011empty list means the strategy succeeded\n          return actions\n\n  # If none of the specialised functions returned a plan, fall back\n  # to a minimal attempt: simply use the USE action (index 4) while\n  # already facing the obstacle.  This may succeed for environments\n  # where no tool is required.\n  return [4]", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
