{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:44:03.771565", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit.  If the wrapper exposes a `max_steps`\n  # attribute we use it, otherwise fall back to a generous default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Pre\u2011compute the list of possible action indices from the action specification.\n  # The spec maps action names (e.g., \"DOWN\") to integer IDs.\n  action_ids = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Choose a random action.  This simple policy does not attempt any planning;\n      # it merely exercises the environment until it terminates.\n      act = np.random.choice(action_ids)\n\n      # Perform the action and collect the result.\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(act)\n      actions.append(int(act))\n\n      # Stop early if the episode reports completion.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
