{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:56:11.847038", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode\n  # The reset call returns the initial observation dictionary,\n  # but we only need it to initialise the environment state.\n  env.reset()\n\n  actions_taken = []\n  done = False\n\n  # Retrieve the possible action indices from the environment.\n  # The action_specs method returns a dict mapping action names to integer ids.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  if not possible_actions:\n      # Fallback to a default action set if the environment does not provide specs.\n      possible_actions = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]  # DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE\n\n  # Run a simple random policy until the episode terminates or a safety limit is reached.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)  # use env.max_steps if present, else cap at 1000\n  while not done and len(actions_taken) < max_steps:\n      # Sample a random action from the available set.\n      action = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n      actions_taken.append(int(action))\n\n      # Step the environment.  The step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(action)\n\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
