{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T13:58:16.760238", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n  done = False\n\n  # Retrieve the list of possible action indices from the environment specification.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Continue taking actions until the episode signals it is done (goal achieved or\n  # maximum steps exhausted).  In the absence of a sophisticated planner we use a\n  # simple random policy.\n  while not done:\n      # Sample a random action from the allowed set.\n      act = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n\n      # Execute the action; the step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(int(act))\n\n      # Safety stop to avoid infinite loops in pathological cases.\n      if len(actions) > 10000:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions performed during the episode.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
