{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:03:09.858387", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Map direction strings to action indices (consistent with CraftLab action specs)\n  dir_to_action = {\"DOWN\": 0, \"UP\": 1, \"LEFT\": 2, \"RIGHT\": 3}\n  move_action = dir_to_action.get(dir.upper())\n  # If the direction is not recognized, we cannot form a valid action sequence.\n  if move_action is None:\n      return []\n  # The environment updates the agent's facing direction when a movement action is taken,\n  # even if the move is blocked by an obstacle. After setting the direction, we issue\n  # the USE action (index 4) to attempt breaking the obstacle in the adjacent cell.\n  return [move_action, 4]", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
