{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:08:03.815010", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random-action policy to collect actions until the task is completed or a step limit is reached.\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  _ = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Retrieve the list of possible action indices from the environment's action specifications.\n  # The action_specs dictionary maps action names (e.g., \"DOWN\", \"UP\", ...) to integer indices.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Define a safety limit to avoid infinite loops in case the environment never reaches a terminal state.\n  max_steps = 1000\n\n  # Loop until the environment signals that the episode is done or the step limit is hit.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Sample a random action from the available actions.\n      action = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n\n      # Execute the action in the environment. The step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(action)\n\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(int(action))\n\n      # If the environment reports that the episode is finished, break out of the loop.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions taken during the episode.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:08:10.054316", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  if not hasattr(env, \"world\") or not hasattr(env.world, \"n_actions\"):\n      return np.array([], dtype=np.int32)\n  return np.zeros(env.world.n_actions, dtype=np.int32)", "env_interactions": 5, "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
