{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:12:05.489919", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Map direction strings to the corresponding action indices defined by CraftLab.\n  dir_to_action = {\n      \"DOWN\": 0,\n      \"UP\": 1,\n      \"LEFT\": 2,\n      \"RIGHT\": 3,\n  }\n\n  # If the provided direction is not recognized, do nothing.\n  if dir not in dir_to_action:\n      return []\n\n  # The simplest breaking strategy: step towards the obstacle and then issue a USE action.\n  # More sophisticated logic (e.g., checking the type of obstacle or crafting a tool)\n  # can be added later, but this baseline works for the generic interface.\n  return [dir_to_action[dir], 4]", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
