{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:18:11.500808", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Initialize the environment and obtain the initial observation.\n  # The reset may accept a seed, but we use the default.\n  _ = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable step limit. Prefer the environment's max_steps\n  # attribute if it exists; otherwise fall back to a default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 2000)\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # If the environment reports that the episode is finished, stop.\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Sample a random valid action.\n      # The world object stores the total number of actions.\n      n_actions = getattr(env.world, \"n_actions\", 5)  # default to 5 actions\n      action = np.random.randint(0, n_actions)\n\n      # Execute the action.\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(action)\n\n      # Record the action.\n      actions.append(int(action))\n\n      # Stop early if the episode terminated.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
