{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:20:44.925839", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n  done = False\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names to integer indices.\n  # This is typically a dict like {\"DOWN\":0, \"UP\":1, \"LEFT\":2, \"RIGHT\":3, \"USE\":4}.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Extract just the integer action IDs for sampling.\n  possible_actions = list(action_map.values())\n\n  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the episode ends\n  # or a safety limit on the number of steps is reached.\n  max_steps = 1000\n  while not done and len(actions) < max_steps:\n      # Choose a random action.\n      action = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n      # Perform the action in the environment.\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(action)\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(action)\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions that were executed.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
