{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:31:13.606196", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  \"\"\"\n  Simple fallback policy for the Craft environment.\n  Executes random actions until the task is completed or the step limit is reached.\n  Returns the list of actions taken.\n  \"\"\"\n  actions = []\n  # Retrieve the maximum allowed steps for the episode\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Obtain the list of possible action integers\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  # Ensure there is at least one action (should always be true)\n  if not possible_actions:\n      return actions\n\n  # Loop until the environment signals done or we exceed max_steps\n  while not env._is_done() and len(actions) < max_steps:\n      # Choose a random action from the available set\n      act = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n      # Apply the action; ignore the returned reward and observation\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n      actions.append(int(act))\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
