{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:38:55.869290", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Mapping of direction strings to movement actions (not used for breaking,\n  # but kept for possible extensions)\n  dir_to_action = {\"DOWN\": 0, \"UP\": 1, \"LEFT\": 2, \"RIGHT\": 3}\n\n  # The USE action index is defined by the environment (always 4 in CraftWorld)\n  USE_ACTION = 4\n\n  # Get the current state from the environment (CraftLab wrapper stores it in\n  # the private attribute `_current_state`).\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Determine the coordinates of the cell adjacent to the agent in the\n  # requested direction.\n  x, y = state.pos\n  if dir == \"DOWN\":\n      nx, ny = x, y + 1\n  elif dir == \"UP\":\n      nx, ny = x, y - 1\n  elif dir == \"LEFT\":\n      nx, ny = x - 1, y\n  elif dir == \"RIGHT\":\n      nx, ny = x + 1, y\n  else:\n      # Unknown direction \u2013 nothing to do.\n      return []\n\n  # Ensure the adjacent cell lies inside the grid.\n  width, height, _ = state.grid.shape\n  if not (0 <= nx < width and 0 <= ny < height):\n      return []\n\n  # Identify which kind(s) occupy the adjacent cell.\n  cell_kinds = np.where(state.grid[nx, ny, :] > 0)[0]\n\n  # If the cell contains any non\u2011grabbable entity (i.e., an obstacle such as\n  # water, stone, or tree), the only possible way to remove it is to issue a\n  # USE action while facing that cell.\n  if any(k in env.world.non_grabbable_indices for k in cell_kinds):\n      return [USE_ACTION]\n\n  # No obstacle to break \u2013 return an empty action list.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
