{"timestamp": "2025-11-04T14:43:09.284713", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  # The observation dictionary contains feature vectors and other info, but we only need\n  # the action space for selecting actions.\n  env.reset()\n  actions_taken = []\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names to integer indices.\n  # This dictionary is stable across steps, so we fetch it once.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  action_indices = list(action_map.values())\n\n  # Define a hard ceiling on the number of steps to avoid infinite loops.\n  # The CraftLab wrapper already enforces a max_steps limit, but we keep our own\n  # safeguard in case the environment is mis\u2011configured.\n  MAX_STEPS = 2000\n\n  for _ in range(MAX_STEPS):\n      # Perform a single step with a randomly chosen action.\n      # The step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      # We ignore the reward because the default CraftLab implementation gives 0\n      # for each step; the important signal is the 'done' flag.\n      chosen_action = np.random.choice(action_indices)\n      _, done, _ = env.step(chosen_action)\n\n      # Record the action for possible debugging or analysis.\n      actions_taken.append(chosen_action)\n\n      # If the environment reports completion (goal reached or step limit hit),\n      # we exit the loop early.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions taken during the episode.\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
